# Check if All A's Appears Before All B's

**Problem:** [LeetCode - Check if All A's Appears Before All B's](https://leetcode.com/problems/check-if-all-as-appears-before-all-bs/)

## Approach: Track Last Occurrences

- Maintain two variables, `last_a` and `last_b`, to store the last occurrence of `'a'` and the first occurrence of `'b'` respectively.
- Traverse the string from both ends.
- If either character is absent, return `true`.
- Otherwise, check whether the first occurrence of `'b'` comes after the last occurrence of `'a'`.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    bool checkString(string s) {
        int last_a = -1, last_b = -1;
        int n = s.length();

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            s[i] == 'a' ? last_a = i : last_a;
            s[n-i-1] == 'b' ? last_b = n-i-1 : last_b;
        }

        if(last_a == -1 || last_b == -1) return true;

        return last_b > last_a;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(n) — Single traversal of the string.
- **Space Complexity:** O(1) — Only two variables are used.
